    "text": "96\n\n Don\u2019t Let Red Lines Derail Your Deal\nHi Sara,\nLet\u2019s talk about a universal truth in deal-making: everyone\u2019s happy with the first draft of a purchase agreement...until those dreaded red lines show up.\nThe initial draft goes out, and spirits are high. It\u2019s a moment of optimism, closing seems within reach and simple. But the second round of edits between the parties\u2019 attorneys? If you\u2019re not careful, that\u2019s when the wheels come off, and chaos ensues. Resentment brews. Tempers flare. Attorneys fees mount and people blame the other side.\u00a0\nWhy does this happen?\nSticker Shock on Legal Fees: Those mounting invoices don\u2019t exactly inspire goodwill.\n\nRejection Stings: When your carefully crafted offer gets marked up or outright rejected, it can feel very personal.\n\nThe Lawyer Factor: Let\u2019s face it, some attorneys are more sandpaper than silk\u2014grating and uncooperative. Add in the \u201ctelephone game\u201d between two parties, and it\u2019s a recipe for escalation.\n\n By this point, the excitement of the deal is a distant memory, replaced by glares across the negotiation table. But it doesn\u2019t have to be this way.\nHow to Keep Your Deal on Track:\nStart Fair: A balanced initial agreement minimizes the back-and-forth drama.\n\nNail the LOI: A solid Letter of intent sets the stage for smoother negotiations in the definitive agreements.\n\nChoose the Right Attorney: A collaborative, experienced deal attorney can save your deal\u2014and your sanity. If you choose a combative attorney or a lawyer who doesn\u2019t primarily work in deals, you may be throwing a wildcard into the mix that the deal can\u2019t recover from.\n\nThe bottom line? A little upfront effort and the right professionals can keep your deal moving forward, even through those inevitable red-line edits.\nHere\u2019s to smarter deals (and friendlier attorneys),\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nBusiness Consultant and Founder of Deal Academy\nFor more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers podcast episodes by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
